  ('shakedown-snowboard-games--2015', 'shakedown-snowboard-games--2015', '2015 Shakedown', 'shakedown-snowboard-games', 2015, '2015-04-04', '2015-04-04', 'contest', 'Last edition listed by the event''s own edition table. SnowboardQuebec''s timeline places a cancelled Shakedown season in its 2015 entry, and CBC reported a Shakedown cancellation in January 2016 for lack of sponsorship and snow; whether the 2015 contest ran and the 2016 one was cancelled is unresolved - see open questions.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Mont Saint-Sauveur', 'Saint-Sauveur', 'Canada', ARRAY['slopestyle','big-air','jib']::text[], ARRAY['https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shakedown_(Snowboard_Games)','https://www.snowboardquebec.com/histoire/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('showcase-showdown--1997', 'showcase-showdown--1997', '1997 Showcase Showdown (first edition)', 'showcase-showdown', 1997, '1997-02-01', '1997-02-01', 'contest', 'Whistler Blackcomb''s 60th anniversary timeline dates the first Showcase Showdown to 1 February 1997. Snowboard Magazine''s billing of the 2015 event as the 18th annual implies a 1998 start instead; the discrepancy is unresolved. The Whistler Museum separately records a Showcase Snowboards halfpipe competition on Blackcomb in 1992, won in the male 18-plus category by Whistler''s Robin Dow, which may be a predecessor.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Blackcomb Mountain', 'Whistler', 'Canada', NULL, ARRAY['https://www.whistlerblackcomb.com/explore-the-resort/discover/whistler-blackcomb-60-anniversary.aspx','https://whistlermuseum.org/2022/04/05/snowboard-park-no-skiers-allowed/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('showcase-showdown--2015', 'showcase-showdown--2015', '18th annual Showcase Showdown', 'showcase-showdown', 2015, '2015-03-14', '2015-03-15', 'contest', 'Big air with a junior rail jam added for the first time. $22,000 in total prizes; $10,000 to the pro men''s winner plus a start in the WSSF Monster Energy Shred Show. Presented by Monster Energy, Burton and Vans, with an after-party featuring Anti-Flag. Snowboard Magazine lists the contest date as Saturday 14 March; the Georgia Straight gives 14-15 March.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Nintendo Terrain Park, Blackcomb Mountain', 'Whistler', 'Canada', ARRAY['big-air','rail-jam']::text[], ARRAY['https://snowboardmag.com/news/whistler-blackcombs-18th-annual-showcase-showdown-returns-march-14','https://www.straight.com/life/402596/showcase-showdown-and-whistler-ski-and-snowboard-fest-go-far-beyond-rock-n-snow']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('sidesurfers-banked-slalom--2026', 'sidesurfers-banked-slalom--2026', '2026 Sidesurfers Banked Slalom', 'sidesurfers-banked-slalom', 2026, '2026-03-21', '2026-03-21', 'contest', 'Dates from a third-party events roundup, not from the organiser.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Sugarbush Resort', 'Warren, Vermont', 'USA', ARRAY['banked-slalom']::text[], ARRAY['https://localfreshies.com/banked-slalom-event-showcase/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('snoboard-shop-north-american-championships--1985', 'snoboard-shop-north-american-championships--1985', '1985 Snoboard Shop North American Snowboarding Championships (first edition)', 'snoboard-shop-north-american-championships', 1985, '1985', NULL, 'contest', 'SnowboardQuebec''s history page states Ken Achenbach''s Snoboard Shop launched the North American Snowboarding Championships in Alberta in 1985 with a $20,000 purse, calling it the first snowboard event held in Canada, and says the series ended in 1988. Venue for 1985 is unconfirmed: the 1987 edition is sourced to Sunshine Village and later accounts describe an annual May long weekend contest there, but the one source naming a 1985 result places the event ''in Calgary''.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', NULL, NULL, 'Canada', ARRAY['other']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.snowboardquebec.com/histoire/','https://snowboarding8090.com/history/','https://kootenaymountainculture.com/meet-the-men-who-brought-snowboarding-to-canada/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('snoboard-shop-north-american-championships--1987', 'snoboard-shop-north-american-championships--1987', '1987 Snoboard Shop North American Championships', 'snoboard-shop-north-american-championships', 1987, '1987-05', '1987-05', 'contest', 'Held on the May long weekend with a $20,000 purse. A photograph of Dave Achenbach from this event ran on the cover of the first issue of TransWorld Snowboarding. Exact dates and the disciplines run were not sourced.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'month', 'Sunshine Village', 'Banff', 'Canada', ARRAY['other']::text[], ARRAY['https://kootenaymountainculture.com/meet-the-men-who-brought-snowboarding-to-canada/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('snowboard-jamboree--2013', 'snowboard-jamboree--2013', '2013 Snowboard Jamboree / FIS Snowboarding World Championships', 'snowboard-jamboree', 2013, '2013-01-18', '2013-01-27', 'contest', 'The 2013 FIS Snowboarding World Championships were staged at Stoneham on these dates. Ski Canada''s 2014 preview describes the 2014 Jamboree as the 9th edition, which places the 2013 festival as the 8th.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Stoneham Mountain Resort', 'Stoneham-et-Tewkesbury', 'Canada', ARRAY['big-air','halfpipe','slopestyle','boardercross','parallel-giant-slalom','parallel-slalom']::text[], ARRAY['https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FIS_Snowboarding_World_Championships_2013','https://www.skicanada.org/snowboard-world-cup-returns-stoneham-quebec-city/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('snowboard-jamboree--2014', 'snowboard-jamboree--2014', '9th Snowboard Jamboree', 'snowboard-jamboree', 2014, '2014-01-16', '2014-01-19', 'contest', 'Billed as the 9th Snowboard Jamboree and the 15th World Cup held in Quebec. First year the event was sanctioned as a 5-star World Snowboard Tour stop and first year it offered three freestyle World Cup disciplines. Last international snowboard competition before the Sochi 2014 Olympics. Stairsmasters video contest returned.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Stoneham Mountain Resort and Quebec City', 'Quebec City', 'Canada', ARRAY['big-air','slopestyle','halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.skicanada.org/snowboard-world-cup-returns-stoneham-quebec-city/','https://www.skicanada.org/stoneham-snowboard-jamboree-now-world-cup-event/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('snowboard-jamboree--2015', 'snowboard-jamboree--2015', '10th Snowboard Jamboree', 'snowboard-jamboree', 2015, '2015-02-19', '2015-02-22', 'contest', '10th edition and the 16th FIS Snowboard World Cup held at the festival. Big air on 20 February at Ilot Fleurie in downtown Quebec City, slopestyle on 21 February at Stoneham. About 200 athletes from more than 20 countries. First time 19 women contested big air at a World Cup here. Stairsmasters video contest ran alongside.', 'verified', 'held', 'The halfpipe World Cup scheduled for 22 February at Stoneham was cancelled: organisers cited a significant lack of snow, warm weather and a labour dispute making an FIS-standard pipe impossible.', 'day', 'Stoneham Mountain Resort and Ilot Fleurie, Quebec City', 'Quebec City', 'Canada', ARRAY['big-air','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://snowboardmag.com/news/quebec-city-snowboard-jamboree-festival-back-for-10th-edition','https://www.snowboardquebec.com/2014/snowboard-jamboree/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('snowboard-jamboree--2016', 'snowboard-jamboree--2016', '2016 Snowboard Jamboree', 'snowboard-jamboree', 2016, '2016-02-12', '2016-02-14', 'contest', 'Moved entirely into downtown Quebec City and cut back to a single big air World Cup, carrying both FIS and TTR World Snowboard Tour points. Maxence Parrot worked on the venue build. Programme also included the Stairsmasters video contest and the IF3 film festival. Organisers described 16 years of World Cup racing in the region and seven consecutive World Cups in Quebec City from 2009.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Ilot Fleurie', 'Quebec City', 'Canada', ARRAY['big-air']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.firsttracksonline.com/2015/10/01/quebecs-world-cup-jamboree-goes-urban/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('snowboard-jamboree--2018', 'snowboard-jamboree--2018', '2018 Jamboree Big Air World Cup Finals', 'snowboard-jamboree', 2018, '2018-03-22', '2018-03-25', 'contest', 'Listed on Canada Snowboard''s 2017-18 domestic calendar as the Jamboree Big Air World Cup Finals.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Quebec City', 'Quebec City', 'Canada', ARRAY['big-air']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.canadasnowboard.ca/en/news/?id=1213']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('snowboard-jamboree--2019', 'snowboard-jamboree--2019', '2019 Jamboree Snowboard and Ski Big Air', 'snowboard-jamboree', 2019, '2019-03-15', '2019-03-17', 'contest', 'Listed on Canada Snowboard''s 2018-19 domestic calendar as the Jamboree Snowboard and Ski Big Air.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Quebec City', 'Quebec City', 'Canada', ARRAY['big-air']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.canadasnowboard.ca/en/news/?id=1259']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('snowboard-masters-japan--2024', 'snowboard-masters-japan--2024', 'SBM BANKED+ 2024', 'snowboard-masters-japan', 2024, '2024-03-29', '2024-03-30', 'contest', 'Open practice Friday 29 March, competition Saturday 30 March. 150 men and 100 women; entrants had to be 18 or over and resident in Japan. Entry JPY 2,000, JPY 1,000 for JSBA/PSA members.', 'verified', 'held', 'Run as a banked slalom rather than SBM''s usual freeride-performance and obstacle-slalom format, because seasonal conditions made it impossible to prepare the standard courses.', 'day', 'Yamabiko B Course, Nozawa Onsen Ski Resort', 'Nozawa Onsen, Nagano', 'Japan', ARRAY['banked-slalom']::text[], ARRAY['https://steep.jp/en/custom/sbmbanked/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('snowboard-world-cup-pre-fis--1991', 'snowboard-world-cup-pre-fis--1991', '1991 Victoria World Cup Japan', 'snowboard-world-cup-pre-fis', 1991, '1991', NULL, 'contest', 'Snowboarder/TransWorld 1990s timeline: the Victoria World Cup Japan at Rusutsu, with over one million dollars spent, was ''the richest contest so far''. No dates, format or podium given. This is a single tour stop, not a full season row.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Rusutsu Resort', 'Rusutsu', 'Japan', NULL, ARRAY['https://www.snowboarder.com/news/snowboard-history-timeline-part-31990s']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('spring-battle--2007', 'spring-battle--2007', 'Absolut Park Spring Battle 2007', 'spring-battle', 2007, '2007-03-31', '2007-04-01', 'contest', 'Sunday ran as the TTR 3-Star event with qualification runs and finals; skate sessions and a party ran alongside.', 'verified', 'held', 'Saturday''s main contest was postponed because of weather and replaced by a Best Trick Session on the last three obstacles.', 'day', 'Absolut Park', 'Flachauwinkl', 'Austria', ARRAY['slopestyle','rail-jam']::text[], ARRAY['https://onboardmag.com/news/snowboarding-events/absolut-park-spring-battle-2007-snowboard.html']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('spring-battle--2025', 'spring-battle--2025', 'Spring Battle 2025', 'spring-battle', 2025, '2025-03-08', '2025-03-12', 'contest', 'WSF Elite Level Event counting for the World Snowboard Points List, EUR 65,000 prize purse. Riders had several days to film single-take runs with follow-cam filmers (no editing permitted), judged afterwards by an international WSF panel. Snowboard slopestyle on the Absolut Park kicker line; Best Trick Rail open to snowboarders and freeskiers in a dedicated jib park. Award ceremony 14 March at Haus Flachau.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Absolut Park', 'Flachauwinkl', 'Austria', ARRAY['slopestyle','rail-jam']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.absolutpark.com/en/spring-battle-25/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('stylewars-australia--2007', 'stylewars-australia--2007', 'Stylewars 007 presented by Oakley', 'stylewars-australia', 2007, '2007-08-27', '2007-09-02', 'contest', 'Swatch TTR 3-Star. Ran the week after the Garnier Fructis Australian Open at Perisher Blue.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Falls Creek', 'Falls Creek, Victoria', 'Australia', ARRAY['slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/events-in-australia/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('stylewars-australia--2010', 'stylewars-australia--2010', 'Stylewars 2010', 'stylewars-australia', 2010, '2010-08-23', '2010-08-25', 'contest', 'Billed by the WSF as Australia''s biggest Swatch TTR tour event (4-Star), drawing riders from across the southern hemisphere.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Falls Creek', 'Falls Creek, Victoria', 'Australia', ARRAY['slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/?s=Stylewars']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('stylewars-australia--2011', 'stylewars-australia--2011', 'Stylewars 2011', 'stylewars-australia', 2011, '2011-08-23', NULL, 'contest', '25 riders. A ''28 Stairs'' rail jam ran alongside. Scotty James, then 17, led after day one; Gjermund Braaten withdrew injured. The WSF report is dated 23 August 2011 and does not name the resort.', 'unverified', 'held', 'Slopestyle scaled back from three days to two.', 'day', NULL, NULL, 'Australia', ARRAY['slopestyle','rail-jam']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/stylewars-2011-australia/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('sugarloaf-banked-slalom--2026', 'sugarloaf-banked-slalom--2026', '2026 Sugarloaf Banked Slalom', 'sugarloaf-banked-slalom', 2026, '2026-03-21', '2026-03-21', 'contest', 'Also referred to as the Mike Baker Banked Slalom. Dates from a third-party events roundup.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Sugarloaf', 'Carrabassett Valley, Maine', 'USA', ARRAY['banked-slalom']::text[], ARRAY['https://localfreshies.com/banked-slalom-event-showcase/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('suomi-tour--2015', 'suomi-tour--2015', 'Suomi Tour 2015', 'suomi-tour', 2015, '2015-02-07', '2015-04-12', 'contest', 'Four stops: Vuokatti (7-8 Feb), Ounasvaara (21-22 Feb), Talma (14-15 Mar) and Ruka (9-12 Apr, run as SM15, the Finnish championships). Grom, Rookie and Open categories; EUR 35 entry with an FSA licence covering the three regional events; Burton Riglet park and coaching for parents and non-competing young riders.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', NULL, NULL, 'Finland', ARRAY['slopestyle','halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/suomi-tour-finland/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('swiss-snowboard-championships--2014', 'swiss-snowboard-championships--2014', 'Swiss Freestyle Snowboard Championships 2014', 'swiss-snowboard-championships', 2014, '2014-04-11', '2014-04-12', 'contest', 'Closing event of the Swiss-Ski Audi Snowboard Series season, and the first time in years that the snowboard freestyle championships were held together with the freeskiers.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Corvatsch', 'Silvaplana, Engadin', 'Switzerland', ARRAY['slopestyle','halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/audi-snowboard-series/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('tenjin-banked-slalom--2012', 'tenjin-banked-slalom--2012', 'Tenjin Banked Slalom 2012', 'tenjin-banked-slalom', 2012, '2012-03-03', '2012-03-04', 'contest', 'Listed by the WSF as Japan''s banked slalom, roughly 1.5 hours from Tokyo. Earliest edition found.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Tenjindaira', 'Minakami, Gunma', 'Japan', ARRAY['banked-slalom']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/wsf-support-banked-slalom-all-around/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('tenjin-banked-slalom--2015', 'tenjin-banked-slalom--2015', 'Tenjin Banked Slalom 2015', 'tenjin-banked-slalom', 2015, '2015-03-07', '2015-03-07', 'contest', 'WSF report says the contest had run for three seasons before this one. Organised by former pro rider Yosuke Nishida, director of the TJ brand, on Mt Tanigawa.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Tenjindaira Ski Resort', 'Minakami, Gunma', 'Japan', ARRAY['banked-slalom']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/2015-tenjin-banked-slalom/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('tenjin-banked-slalom--2016', 'tenjin-banked-slalom--2016', 'Tenjin Banked Slalom 2016', 'tenjin-banked-slalom', 2016, '2016-03-05', '2016-03-06', 'contest', 'Heats on 5 March in clear weather, finals over two runs on 6 March. Course deliberately balanced for regular and goofy riders; based out of the Canyons lodge at the resort base. Snowboard brands demoed 2016/17 models alongside.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Tenjin Ski Resort', 'Minakami, Gunma', 'Japan', ARRAY['banked-slalom']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/photogallery-and-results-from-2016-tenjin-banked-slalom/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('tenjin-banked-slalom--2017', 'tenjin-banked-slalom--2017', 'Tenjin Banked Slalom 2017', 'tenjin-banked-slalom', 2017, '2017-03-04', '2017-03-05', 'contest', 'Over 400 people across the two days. Opened with a traditional ceremony praying for safety, reflecting the mountain''s avalanche history. Riders received a TBS x Volcom collaboration T-shirt.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Tenjindaira', 'Minakami, Gunma', 'Japan', ARRAY['banked-slalom']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/tenjin-banked-slalom-2017/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('the-arctic-challenge--1999', 'the-arctic-challenge--1999', 'The Arctic Challenge 1999 (pilot)', 'the-arctic-challenge', 1999, '1999', NULL, 'contest', 'Pilot project: Terje Haakonsen, Daniel Franck and Oakley invited 12 riders to Norway to test the concept. Halfpipe in Trysil, surfing and freeriding in Lofoten. Terje later described 2014 as ''15 years since we did the pilot event''.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Trysil and Lofoten', NULL, 'Norway', ARRAY['halfpipe','freeride','other']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.the-house.com/portal/the-history-of-the-oakley-arctic-challenge/','https://whitelines.com/archive/news/terje-haakonsen-releases-new-statement-on-the-arctic-challenge.html']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('the-arctic-challenge--2000', 'the-arctic-challenge--2000', 'The Arctic Challenge 2000', 'the-arctic-challenge', 2000, '2000', NULL, 'contest', 'First full competition: halfpipe, quarterpipe, surf, skate and freeride.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Lofoten', NULL, 'Norway', ARRAY['halfpipe','quarterpipe','freeride','other']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.the-house.com/portal/the-history-of-the-oakley-arctic-challenge/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('the-arctic-challenge--2001', 'the-arctic-challenge--2001', 'The Arctic Challenge 2001', 'the-arctic-challenge', 2001, '2001', NULL, 'contest', 'Moved south because of weather: halfpipe at Hemsedal, quarterpipe at Holmenkollen in Oslo. Heikki Sorsa set a 9.3 m quarterpipe air record at this event.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Hemsedal and Holmenkollen', NULL, 'Norway', ARRAY['halfpipe','quarterpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.the-house.com/portal/the-history-of-the-oakley-arctic-challenge/','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctic_Challenge']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('the-arctic-challenge--2002', 'the-arctic-challenge--2002', 'The Arctic Challenge 2002', 'the-arctic-challenge', 2002, '2002', NULL, 'contest', NULL, 'verified', 'cancelled', 'Cancelled after the sports marketing firm Sportsworld went bankrupt; Terje Haakonsen personally took on the financial obligations.', 'year', NULL, NULL, 'Norway', NULL, ARRAY['https://www.the-house.com/portal/the-history-of-the-oakley-arctic-challenge/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('the-arctic-challenge--2003', 'the-arctic-challenge--2003', 'The Arctic Challenge 2003', 'the-arctic-challenge', 2003, '2003', NULL, 'contest', NULL, 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Trysil', 'Trysil', 'Norway', ARRAY['halfpipe','quarterpipe','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.the-house.com/portal/the-history-of-the-oakley-arctic-challenge/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('the-arctic-challenge--2004', 'the-arctic-challenge--2004', 'The Arctic Challenge 2004', 'the-arctic-challenge', 2004, '2004', NULL, 'contest', 'Halfpipe and quarterpipe plus a music and lifestyle programme.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', NULL, 'Tromsø', 'Norway', ARRAY['halfpipe','quarterpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.the-house.com/portal/the-history-of-the-oakley-arctic-challenge/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('the-arctic-challenge--2005', 'the-arctic-challenge--2005', 'The Arctic Challenge 2005', 'the-arctic-challenge', 2005, '2005-03-29', '2005-04-06', 'contest', 'Last edition held above the Arctic Circle; from 2006 the event moved to the Oslo area. Show sessions replaced the cancelled contests.', 'verified', 'held', 'Arctic storms forced relocations; the halfpipe and slopestyle were cancelled and only the Tromsø quarterpipe ran, in pouring rain.', 'day', 'Tromsø, Finnsnes and Stamsund', 'Tromsø', 'Norway', ARRAY['halfpipe','quarterpipe','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.the-arctic-challenge.com/','https://www.the-house.com/portal/the-history-of-the-oakley-arctic-challenge/','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctic_Challenge']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('the-arctic-challenge--2006', 'the-arctic-challenge--2006', 'The Arctic Challenge 2006', 'the-arctic-challenge', 2006, '2006', NULL, 'contest', 'First edition in Oslo.', 'verified', 'held', 'Major weather delays; scaffolding had to be replaced before the event.', 'year', NULL, 'Oslo', 'Norway', NULL, ARRAY['https://www.the-house.com/portal/the-history-of-the-oakley-arctic-challenge/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('the-arctic-challenge--2007', 'the-arctic-challenge--2007', 'The Arctic Challenge 2007', 'the-arctic-challenge', 2007, '2007-03-02', NULL, 'contest', 'Terje Haakonsen set a quarterpipe air record of 9.8 m above the lip, beating Heikki Sorsa''s 9.3 m from 2001. Venue not stated in the sources I opened. [QA-corrected: venue and date taken from the cited the-house.com history, which the original row overlooked.]', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Oslo', NULL, 'Norway', ARRAY['quarterpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.the-house.com/portal/the-history-of-the-oakley-arctic-challenge/','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctic_Challenge']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('the-arctic-challenge--2008', 'the-arctic-challenge--2008', 'Oakley Arctic Challenge 2008', 'the-arctic-challenge', 2008, '2008', NULL, 'contest', 'About 7,000 spectators in good weather.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Holmenkollen', 'Oslo', 'Norway', NULL, ARRAY['https://www.the-house.com/portal/the-history-of-the-oakley-arctic-challenge/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('the-arctic-challenge--2010', 'the-arctic-challenge--2010', 'Oakley Arctic Challenge 2010', 'the-arctic-challenge', 2010, '2010-03-04', '2010-03-07', 'contest', 'TTR 6Star slopestyle. Practice and a downtown Oslo grand opening on Thursday 4 March, semi-finals Saturday 6 March, finals Sunday 7 March; capacity 4,000. Course shaper Claes Hoegstrom. Peetu Piiroinen''s win here secured the Swatch TTR world title.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', NULL, 'Oslo', 'Norway', ARRAY['slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/the-oakley-arctic-challenge/','https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/ttr-winner-of-oakley-arctic-challenge-petuu-piiroinen-secures-swatch-ttr-world/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('the-arctic-challenge--2011', 'the-arctic-challenge--2011', 'Oakley Arctic Challenge 2011', 'the-arctic-challenge', 2011, '2011-02-14', '2011-02-19', 'contest', '6Star slopestyle with 30 men and 16 women and a USD 100,000 purse; qualification from the TTR ranking (top 20 men, top 10 women after the Burton European Open), qualifying events and wildcards. Staged as the trial run for the 2012 World Snowboarding Championships.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Oslo Vinterpark', 'Oslo', 'Norway', ARRAY['slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/the-oakley-arctic-challenge-announces-2011-rider-protocol/','https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/oakley-arctic-challenge/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('the-arctic-challenge--2013', 'the-arctic-challenge--2013', 'The Arctic Challenge 2013', 'the-arctic-challenge', 2013, '2013', '2013-03-09', 'contest', 'Main snowboard event on 9 March 2013, with a halfpipe competition (snowboard and freestyle ski) five days earlier; the volunteer call covered 6-13 March. Start date not stated explicitly.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Tryvann vinterpark', 'Oslo', 'Norway', ARRAY['halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/wanted-helping-hands-for-the-arctic-challenge/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('the-arctic-challenge--2014', 'the-arctic-challenge--2014', 'The Arctic Challenge 2014', 'the-arctic-challenge', 2014, '2014-03-15', '2014-03-15', 'contest', 'Rider-designed format: 12 riders arrived 11 March and had the pipe from 12-15 March to decide the arena and contest format themselves, with the public event on Saturday 15 March. Judged on skill, amplitude and creativity rather than a standard run score. 15 years after the 1999 pilot.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', NULL, 'Oslo', 'Norway', ARRAY['halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://whitelines.com/archive/news/terje-haakonsen-releases-new-statement-on-the-arctic-challenge.html','https://snowboardmag.com/videos/arctic-challenge-2014-terje-haakonsons-vision','https://thesnowboardersjournal.com/blogs/curated-content/the-arctic-challenge-2014-redefining-transition-contests-with-terje-haakonsen']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('the-brits--2009', 'the-brits--2009', 'The BRITS 2009 (20th birthday)', 'the-brits', 2009, '2009-03-28', '2009-04-04', 'contest', '20th birthday edition, billed by the WSF as Europe''s longest established winter snowsports festival. Hosted the British Snowboard and Freeski Championships across kids, rookie, pro and Olympian fields; a skiercross ran alongside.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Laax', 'Laax, Graubuenden', 'Switzerland', ARRAY['boardercross','big-air','slopestyle','halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/news/the-brits-2009-in-laax/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('the-brits--2023', 'the-brits--2023', 'The BRITS 2023', 'the-brits', 2023, '2023-04-01', '2023-04-02', 'contest', 'First return to Scotland in 32 years. Ran as the TSA British Snowboard Championships alongside the Ellis Brigham British Freeski Championships. Cairngorm built the first British halfpipe in 1991.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Cairngorm Mountain', 'Aviemore, Scotland', 'United Kingdom', ARRAY['slopestyle','banked-slalom','rail-jam']::text[], ARRAY['https://planetski.eu/2023/02/02/the-brits-heads-back-to-its-roots-in-scotland/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('toyota-big-air--1997', 'toyota-big-air--1997', '1st Toyota Big Air', 'toyota-big-air', 1997, '1997', NULL, 'contest', 'Inaugural edition. Editions were normally held around 11 February.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Makomanai Open Stadium', 'Sapporo', 'Japan', ARRAY['big-air']::text[], ARRAY['https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/TOYOTA_BIG_AIR','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toyota_Big_Air']::text[], 'verified'),
