  ('toyota-big-air--2014', 'toyota-big-air--2014', '18th Toyota Big Air', 'toyota-big-air', 2014, '2014-02-23', '2014-02-23', 'contest', 'Final edition. The organising office announced on 30 September 2014 that the event would not continue. Date of 23 February 2014 taken from the English Wikipedia article; the Japanese article gives no per-edition dates.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Sapporo Dome', 'Sapporo', 'Japan', ARRAY['big-air']::text[], ARRAY['https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toyota_Big_Air','https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/TOYOTA_BIG_AIR']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2003', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2003', '2002/03 TTR Pro Snowboarding Series season', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour', 2003, '2003', NULL, 'contest', 'First TTR season: nine events worldwide with the Arctic Challenge as the final stop, each event awarding one TTR Medallion and an Arctic Challenge invite. No women''s tour until 2005/06. Events: Nissan X-Trail Jam, Nokia Air & Style, O''Neill SB Jam, Burton European Open, Champs Open, Vans Triple Crown of Snowboarding, The Battle, Quiksilver Slopestyle Pro, US Open.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', NULL, NULL, 'multiple', NULL, ARRAY['https://web.archive.org/web/20220302222719/https://worldsnowboardtour.com/history/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2004', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2004', '2003/04 TTR Pro Snowboarding Series season', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour', 2004, '2004', NULL, 'contest', 'Same nine events as the previous season; the nine TTR medallion winners were invited to the Arctic Challenge, again the tour final.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', NULL, NULL, 'multiple', NULL, ARRAY['https://web.archive.org/web/20220302222719/https://worldsnowboardtour.com/history/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2005', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2005', '2004/05 TTR World Snowboard Tour season', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour', 2005, '2005', NULL, 'contest', 'Season edition rows use the calendar year the season ended. The Arctic Challenge''s own 2005 site published the 2004/2005 TTR Tour standings, with Andy Finch as overall champion, which confirms the season ran.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', NULL, NULL, 'multiple', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','big-air','quarterpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.the-arctic-challenge.com/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2006', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2006', '2005/06 TTR World Snowboard Tour season', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour', 2006, '2006', NULL, 'contest', 'Introduction of the 1-6Star tier system, the TTR ranking system, the first TTR website (ttrworldtour.com) and the official Women''s Tour. 67 events in total. The TTR World Ranking list launched 5 December 2005 and the first-ever TTR World Tour Champions were crowned at the US Open.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', NULL, NULL, 'multiple', NULL, ARRAY['https://web.archive.org/web/20220302222719/https://worldsnowboardtour.com/history/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2007', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2007', '2006/07 TTR World Snowboard Tour season', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour', 2007, '2007', NULL, 'contest', 'First season with a dedicated women''s tour, announced 24 October 2006. WSF described a provisional women''s calendar of over 20 events offering more than 30 possible results, kicking off with the Burton Abominable Snow Jam at Mt Hood in July 2006 and ending at the Roxy Chicken Jam Finals in Park City, 22-25 March 2007. The Billabong Pro Junior in Australia and the Burton Australian Open were cancelled for poor snow.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', NULL, NULL, 'multiple', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','big-air','quarterpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/ttr-women-tour-announced/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2008', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2008', '2007/08 Swatch TTR World Snowboard Tour season', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour', 2008, '2008', NULL, 'contest', 'Introduction of a $250,000 end-of-season prize purse. 176 results registered across four formats from events in 27 nations; 3,417 riders (2,706 men, 711 women) from 41 nations ranked.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', NULL, NULL, 'multiple', NULL, ARRAY['https://web.archive.org/web/20220302222719/https://worldsnowboardtour.com/history/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2009', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2009', '2008/09 Swatch TTR World Snowboard Tour season', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour', 2009, '2009', NULL, 'contest', 'First of Peetu Piiroinen''s three consecutive men''s overall titles, per Guinness World Records.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', NULL, NULL, 'multiple', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','big-air','quarterpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/102159-most-men%E2%80%99s-ttr-world-snowboard-tour-titles']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2010', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2010', '2009/10 Swatch TTR World Snowboard Tour season', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour', 2010, '2010', NULL, 'contest', 'Second of Peetu Piiroinen''s three consecutive men''s overall titles; WSF reported he secured the Swatch TTR world title by winning the Oakley Arctic Challenge in March 2010.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', NULL, NULL, 'multiple', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','big-air','quarterpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/102159-most-men%E2%80%99s-ttr-world-snowboard-tour-titles','https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/ttr-winner-of-oakley-arctic-challenge-petuu-piiroinen-secures-swatch-ttr-world/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2011', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2011', '2010/11 Swatch TTR World Snowboard Tour season', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour', 2011, '2011', NULL, 'contest', 'Third of Peetu Piiroinen''s three consecutive men''s overall titles, per Guinness World Records.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', NULL, NULL, 'multiple', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','big-air','quarterpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/102159-most-men%E2%80%99s-ttr-world-snowboard-tour-titles']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2012', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2012', '2011/12 World Snowboard Tour season', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour', 2012, '2012', NULL, 'contest', 'TTR''s 10th anniversary season. Highlight was the inaugural World Snowboarding Championships at Oslo Vinterpark in February 2012, developed and owned by TTR and the World Snowboard Federation and run as a 6Star tour event - the first world championships organised by snowboarders since 1999. The Burton European Open was postponed to March, making WCS qualification difficult.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', NULL, NULL, 'multiple', NULL, ARRAY['https://web.archive.org/web/20220302222719/https://worldsnowboardtour.com/history/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2013', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2013', '2012/13 World Snowboard Tour season', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour', 2013, '2013', NULL, 'contest', 'First season under the new name. TTR announced on 2-4 July 2012 that the TTR World Tour would be called the World Snowboard Tour from the 2012/13 season; TTR president Reto Lamm said the tour then covered around 350 events across five continents. Headline events named in the announcement were Air & Style Beijing and Innsbruck, Burton European and US Open, O''Neill Evolution Davos and The Arctic Challenge Oslo.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', NULL, NULL, 'multiple', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','big-air','quarterpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/news/ttr-world-tour-becomes-world-snowboard-tour/','https://whitelines.com/archive/news/ttr-rebrands-to-world-snowboard-tour.html']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2014', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2014', '2013/14 World Snowboard Tour season', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour', 2014, '2014', NULL, 'contest', 'Season in which the six star tiers were replaced by four event categories: Regional, National, International and Elite.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', NULL, NULL, 'multiple', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','big-air']::text[], ARRAY['https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/TTR_World_Snowboard_Tour']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2015', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2015', '2014/15 World Snowboard Tour season', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour', 2015, '2015', NULL, 'contest', 'First season under the new tour concept agreed at the May 2014 General Assembly in Barcelona: six star tiers replaced by four categories (Regional, National, International, Elite), with the Elite events forming the WST Pro Series. Titles were awarded in slopestyle and halfpipe only, at the Burton US Open on 8 March 2015.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', NULL, NULL, 'multiple', NULL, ARRAY['https://web.archive.org/web/20220302222719/https://worldsnowboardtour.com/history/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2017', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour--2017', '2016/17 World Snowboard Tour season', 'ttr-world-snowboard-tour', 2017, '2017', NULL, 'contest', 'TTR Pro Snowboarding restricted access to the World Snowboard Points List in January 2017 to force the snowboard industry to fund it. The merger with the WSF was announced 25 May 2017; from the 2017/18 season the merged organisation offered direct membership and the World Snowboard Tour brand ceased to exist.', 'verified', 'held', 'Final season before the tour brand was retired.', 'year', NULL, NULL, 'multiple', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','big-air']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.sgieurope.com/world-snowboarding-will-replace-the-world-snowboard-tour/60795.article','https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/ttr-pro-snowboarding-and-world-snowboard-federation-create-one-joint-organisation/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1982', 'us-open-snowboarding--1982', '1982 National Snowsurfing Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1982, '1982-02-13', '1982-02-13', 'contest', 'Organised by Paul Graves. Doug Bouton won. Burton''s own history page opens the US Open lineage with this event; the PSIA-AASI archive treats it as a separate contest from the National Snowboarding Championships Jake Burton Carpenter organised at Snow Valley the following year. Recorded here as the first row of the lineage with the dispute unresolved.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Suicide Six', 'Woodstock', 'USA', ARRAY['slalom','giant-slalom','downhill','other']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://thesnowpros.org/2024/09/from-the-archives-great-moments-in-snowboarding-history-part-2/','https://www.burton.com/en-us/blogs/the-burton-blog/13-firsts-us-open-snowboarding-championships','https://www.snurferboy.com/nationalchampionship','http://www.snowboardinginsouthernvermont.com/woodstock-1982.html','https://www.snowboarder.com/news/snowboard-history-timeline-part-21980s','https://vermontbiz.com/news/2021/november/02/40-years-later-how-first-snowboarding-event-1982-woodstock-shaped-sport']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1983', 'us-open-snowboarding--1983', '1983 National Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1983, '1983', NULL, 'contest', 'No lift access; competitors hiked the hill. Andy Coghlan won men''s slalom and downhill. Several sources describe this, not 1982, as the first edition of what became the US Open, and Burton''s own later edition numbering (2002 = 20th, 2009 = 27th, 2012 = 30th, 2020 = 38th) counts from 1983.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Snow Valley', 'Winhall', 'USA', ARRAY['slalom','downhill']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://thesnowpros.org/2024/09/from-the-archives-great-moments-in-snowboarding-history-part-2/','https://www.firsttracksonline.com/2002/03/03/the-u-s-open-snowboarding-championships-back-to-where-it-all-began/','https://www.snowboarder.com/news/snowboard-history-timeline-part-21980s']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1984', 'us-open-snowboarding--1984', '1984 National Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1984, '1984', NULL, 'contest', 'Final year at Snow Valley. Andy Coghlan repeated in slalom and downhill.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Snow Valley', 'Winhall', 'USA', ARRAY['slalom','downhill']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1985', 'us-open-snowboarding--1985', '1985 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1985, '1985', NULL, 'contest', 'First year at Stratton Mountain and the year the event was formally called the US Open Snowboarding Championships. Riders began wearing speed suits. Tom Sims won men''s slalom; Andy Coghlan defended the downhill.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['slalom','downhill']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://www.burton.com/en-us/blogs/the-burton-blog/13-firsts-us-open-snowboarding-championships','https://www.skihall.com/hall-of-famers/tom-sims/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1986', 'us-open-snowboarding--1986', '1986 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1986, '1986', NULL, 'contest', 'Over 200 competitors in the pre-qualifiers. Andy Coghlan won slalom and downhill again.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['slalom','downhill']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1987', 'us-open-snowboarding--1987', '1987 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1987, '1987', NULL, 'contest', 'Craig Kelly won the men''s slalom.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['slalom']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1988', 'us-open-snowboarding--1988', '1988 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1988, '1988', NULL, 'contest', 'Halfpipe debuted at the US Open and was immediately treated as the benchmark for competition pipes. Craig Kelly took the overall title. An ice storm preceded the event.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slalom']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://www.burton.com/en-us/blogs/the-burton-blog/13-firsts-us-open-snowboarding-championships']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1989', 'us-open-snowboarding--1989', '1989 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1989, '1989', NULL, 'contest', 'Last year the downhill was run. Craig Kelly won the Overall title. [QA-corrected: the cited sources say halfpipe DEBUTED at the 1989 US Open and that Kelly took the Overall title; the earlier claim of a second consecutive halfpipe title was unsupported. The downhill discipline was uncited and has been removed.]', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1990', 'us-open-snowboarding--1990', '1990 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1990, '1990', NULL, 'contest', 'Terje Haakonsen''s US Open halfpipe debut. Craig Kelly won, against a field including Shaun Palmer and Jeff Brushie.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1991', 'us-open-snowboarding--1991', '1991 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1991, '1991', NULL, 'contest', 'Crowd and competitor numbers roughly doubled. Inverts ridden in competition for the first time. Janna Meyen won the women''s halfpipe over Tina Basich.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1992', 'us-open-snowboarding--1992', '1992 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1992, '1992', NULL, 'contest', 'Terje Haakonsen won the men''s halfpipe; Tricia Byrnes won the women''s.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1993', 'us-open-snowboarding--1993', '1993 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1993, '1993', NULL, 'contest', 'Fresh snow and clear skies. Terje Haakonsen took a second consecutive halfpipe title on his new Burton pro model.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1994', 'us-open-snowboarding--1994', '1994 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1994, '1994', NULL, 'contest', 'Shannon Dunn and Todd Richards won the halfpipes. Terje Haakonsen sat out with an ankle injury.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1995', 'us-open-snowboarding--1995', '1995 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1995, '1995', NULL, 'contest', 'Big air debuted at the US Open. Terje Haakonsen won a third halfpipe title. Victoria Jealouse won the women''s super-G, recorded here as discipline ''other'' because super-G is not in the Linestry discipline vocabulary.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','big-air','other']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1996', 'us-open-snowboarding--1996', '1996 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1996, '1996', NULL, 'contest', 'Held in the season snowboarding''s inclusion in the 1998 Nagano Olympics was announced. Peter Line and Cara-Beth Burnside won big air; Jimi Scott and Satu Jarvela won halfpipe.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','big-air']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1997', 'us-open-snowboarding--1997', '1997 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1997, '1997', NULL, 'contest', 'Reported crowd of over 10,000 for the halfpipe. Todd Richards edged Terje Haakonsen; Barrett Christy won the women''s pipe.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','big-air']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1998', 'us-open-snowboarding--1998', '1998 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1998, '1998', NULL, 'contest', 'Remembered as ''the Year of the Mist'' for heavy fog. Boardercross debuted. Rob Kingwill won the men''s halfpipe; Nicola Thost, the 1998 Olympic champion, won the women''s. Mike Michalchuk''s back-to-back 1620s are cited by Burton as an early double-cork-era moment.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','big-air','boardercross']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://www.burton.com/en-us/blogs/the-burton-blog/13-firsts-us-open-snowboarding-championships']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--1999', 'us-open-snowboarding--1999', '1999 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 1999, '1999', NULL, 'contest', 'Ross Powers won the men''s halfpipe with McTwists and 900s; Nicola Thost won the women''s for a second consecutive year.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2000', 'us-open-snowboarding--2000', '2000 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2000, '2000', NULL, 'contest', 'First superpipe at the US Open, reported as roughly 300 feet long with 15-foot walls. Guillaume Morisset and Natasza Zurek won for Canada. Recorded as halfpipe; the pipe event was run as a superpipe from this year.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2001', 'us-open-snowboarding--2001', '2001 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2001, '2001', NULL, 'contest', 'Danny Kass won the men''s halfpipe, narrowly over Vermont''s Abe Teter. Natasza Zurek took a second consecutive women''s title.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2002', 'us-open-snowboarding--2002', '2002 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2002, '2002-03-14', '2002-03-17', 'contest', 'Held a month after the Salt Lake City Olympics, with a reported 30,000-plus spectators. Kelly Clark won quarterpipe and halfpipe; Danny Kass defended the men''s halfpipe. First Tracks called it the 20th year of the competition, which counts from 1983. [v0.2: MountainZone reports the first US Open slopestyle finals on 17 March 2002, with both podiums; discipline list corrected.]', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','quarterpipe','boardercross','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://www.firsttracksonline.com/2002/03/03/the-u-s-open-snowboarding-championships-back-to-where-it-all-began/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2003', 'us-open-snowboarding--2003', '2003 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2003, '2003-03-11', '2003-03-16', 'contest', 'First rail jam at the US Open, won by Travis Rice; first live television broadcast; Philips became the first title sponsor. Ross Powers won the halfpipe, Gretchen Bleiler the women''s, Shaun White the slopestyle. MountainZone''s contemporaneous slopestyle report is dated 2003-03-15; full event dates not sourced. [v0.3 archive: Open Championships of Snowboarding 2003 calendar: "Mar 11 - 16, 2003 Stratton, VT". The usopen03 schedule page confirms Rail Jam final Friday 14 March, halfpipe finals Saturday 15 March, slopestyle finals Sunday 16 March.] [v0.3 archive: Open Championships of Snowboarding 2003 calendar: "Mar 11 - 16, 2003 Stratton, VT". The usopen03 schedule page confirms Rail Jam final Friday 14 March, halfpipe finals Saturday 15 March, slopestyle finals Sunday 16 March.]', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','rail-jam']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://www.mountainzone.com/2003/usopen/html/usopen_slopestyle.html','https://web.archive.org/web/20030205093000/http://www.opensnowboarding.com/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2004', 'us-open-snowboarding--2004', '2004 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2004, '2004-03-16', '2004-03-21', 'contest', 'Women rode the rail jam for the first time; Leanne Pelosi won. Danny Kass won the halfpipe and the overall title; Kelly Clark won the women''s halfpipe. Priscilla Levac and Jake Blauvelt won slopestyle. [v0.3 archive: 2004 Open Championships of Snowboarding calendar: "Philips US Open March 16-21, 2004 Stratton, VT USA".] [v0.3 archive: 2004 Open Championships of Snowboarding calendar: "Philips US Open March 16-21, 2004 Stratton, VT USA".]', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','rail-jam']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://web.archive.org/web/20040205215129/http://www.opensnowboarding.com/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2005', 'us-open-snowboarding--2005', '2005 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2005, '2005-03-14', '2005-03-20', 'contest', 'Danny Kass became the first rider to win four US Open halfpipe titles. Janna Meyen won her first title since 1991. [v0.3 archive: Open Championships of Snowboarding calendar: "US Open Mar. 14-20, 2005 Stratton, VT USA". The usopen05 schedule page runs Monday March 14th (practice) to Sunday March 20th.] [v0.3 archive: Open Championships of Snowboarding calendar: "US Open Mar. 14-20, 2005 Stratton, VT USA". The usopen05 schedule page runs Monday March 14th (practice) to Sunday March 20th.]', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','rail-jam']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://web.archive.org/web/20050113043806/http://www.opensnowboarding.com/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2006', 'us-open-snowboarding--2006', '2006 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2006, '2006-03-14', '2006-03-19', 'contest', 'Shaun White won halfpipe and slopestyle. The quarterpipe was revived, won by Danny Davis and Hana Beaman. White and Beaman took Most Valuable Rider awards. [v0.3 archive: Open Championships of Snowboarding calendar: "US Open March 14-19, 2006 Stratton, VT USA".] [v0.3 archive: Open Championships of Snowboarding calendar: "US Open March 14-19, 2006 Stratton, VT USA".]', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','quarterpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://web.archive.org/web/20060213052702/http://www.opensnowboarding.com/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2007', 'us-open-snowboarding--2007', '2007 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2007, '2007-03-12', '2007-03-18', 'contest', 'Marked by Burton as the 25th anniversary. Shaun White and Torah Bright won the first Burton Global Open Series championship titles, USD 100,000 each. Kelly Clark won a third halfpipe title; Travis Rice and Jamie Anderson won slopestyle. [v0.3 archive: Burton Global Open Series press release: "US Open March 12-18, 2007 Stratton, VT, USA".] [v0.3 archive: Burton Global Open Series press release: "US Open March 12-18, 2007 Stratton, VT, USA".]', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://web.archive.org/web/20061104145301/http://www.opensnowboarding.com/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2008', 'us-open-snowboarding--2008', '2008 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2008, '2008-03', '2008-03-22', 'contest', 'Total prize purse reported at USD 471,500. Rated 6Star on the Swatch TTR World Snowboard Tour. Slopestyle finals ran 2008-03-21 (Shaun White and Kjersti Buaas) with halfpipe finals the following day; the event''s start date was not sourced. Cheryl Maas and Tim Humphreys won big air.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'month', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','big-air']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/burton-us-open-report/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2009', 'us-open-snowboarding--2009', '2009 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2009, '2009-03-16', '2009-03-22', 'contest', 'Closing event of the 2008/09 Burton Global Open Series; dates as announced in the series calendar. AlpineZone called it the 27th US Open. Danny Kass won a record fifth halfpipe title; Torah Bright won a third. Chas Guldemond and Kjersti Buaas won slopestyle. A best trick contest and a junior jam were also run, recorded as ''other''.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','quarterpipe','other']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://whitelines.com/archive/news/burton-global-open-series-08-09.html','https://www.alpinezone.com/news-and-featured-articles/local-stratton-riders-make-a-splash-at-the-27th-u-s-open-snowboarding-championships/']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2010', 'us-open-snowboarding--2010', '2010 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2010, '2010-03-16', '2010-03-21', 'contest', 'Halfpipe finals ran 2010-03-20 in a slushy pipe; full event dates not sourced. Kazuhiro Kokubo won his first halfpipe title and Kelly Clark became the first woman to win four. Mikkel Bang and Sina Candrian won slopestyle. [v0.3 archive: Burton Global Open Series calendar listed the US Open as March 16-21, 2010. Refines the existing 2010-03 value.] [v0.3 archive: Burton Global Open Series calendar listed the US Open as March 16-21, 2010. Refines the existing 2010-03 value.] [v0.3 QA: the archive citation was a Flash-only page containing no dates and has been removed. The dates rest on the live-web sources.]', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://www.snowboarder.com/news/2010-us-open-halfpipe-results-and-photos']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2011', 'us-open-snowboarding--2011', '2011 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2011, '2011-03-07', '2011-03-13', 'contest', 'Kazuhiro Kokubo won a second consecutive halfpipe title and dedicated it to tsunami-hit Japan. Kelly Clark won a fifth consecutive halfpipe title and her first Burton Global Open Series championship. Eric Willett and Enni Rukajarvi won their first slopestyle titles.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','rail-jam']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://www.worldsnowboardguide.com/events/burton-us-open-2011.html']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2012', 'us-open-snowboarding--2012', '2012 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2012, '2012-03-05', '2012-03-11', 'contest', 'Last US Open at Stratton after 28 editions there. Hit by a freak snowstorm. Shaun White won halfpipe; Elena Hight ended Kelly Clark''s streak; Seb Toots and Jamie Anderson won slopestyle; Chas Guldemond and Kjersti Buaas won The Jam. A veterans'' race, the Washed Up Cup, was run on the Friday night.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Stratton Mountain', 'Stratton', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','rail-jam']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://www.methodmag.com/events/burton-us-open-2012.html']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2013', 'us-open-snowboarding--2013', '2013 US Open Snowboarding Championships', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2013, '2013-02-25', '2013-03-02', 'contest', 'First US Open at Vail after 28 years in Vermont. Over USD 340,000 in prize money. Mark McMorris won his first slopestyle title, Spencer O''Brien the women''s; Shaun White won the halfpipe with 14-year-old Ayumu Hirano second.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Vail Mountain', 'Vail', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/','https://snowboardmag.com/stories/burton-us-open-snowboarding-championships-announces-schedule-and-formats']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2014', 'us-open-snowboarding--2014', '32nd Burton US Open (2014)', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2014, '2014-03-03', '2014-03-08', 'contest', 'Slopestyle finals 2014-03-07, halfpipe finals 2014-03-08. Mark McMorris won a second consecutive slopestyle; Jamie Anderson won the women''s; Kelly Clark won the halfpipe.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Vail Mountain', 'Vail', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://snowboardmag.com/stories/2014-burton-us-open-snowboarding-championships-roster','https://shop-eat-surf-outdoor.com/news/2014-03-relive-the-32nd-burton-us-open-on-burton-com-and-fox-sports-2/27965/','https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2015', 'us-open-snowboarding--2015', '33rd Burton US Open (2015)', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2015, '2015-03-02', '2015-03-07', 'contest', 'Yuki Kadono won men''s slopestyle with back-to-back triple cork 1620s, reported as a competition first. Jamie Anderson won a fourth slopestyle title; Kelly Clark won an eighth halfpipe title; Taku Hiraoka won the men''s halfpipe.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Vail Mountain', 'Vail', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://news.vailresorts.com/2015-01-22-The-2015-Burton-US-Open-Announces-World-Class-Entertainment-Line-Up','https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2016', 'us-open-snowboarding--2016', '34th Burton US Open (2016)', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2016, '2016-02-29', '2016-03-05', 'contest', 'USD 343,000 prize purse. Shaun White returned to the halfpipe podium; 15-year-old Chloe Kim won her first halfpipe title. Jamie Anderson and Kyle Mack won slopestyle. Junior jam halfpipe on 2016-03-01.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Vail Mountain', 'Vail', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://snowboardmag.com/news/the-2016-burton-us-open-snowboarding-championships-return-to-vail-february-29-march-5','https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2017', 'us-open-snowboarding--2017', '35th Burton US Open (2017)', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2017, '2017-02-27', '2017-03-04', 'contest', 'Anna Gasser won her first title in women''s slopestyle; Mark McMorris won the men''s. Shaun White and Chloe Kim defended their halfpipe titles. Junior jam halfpipe for riders 14 and under.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Vail Mountain', 'Vail', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.snowboarder.com/transworld-snowboarding-archive/snowboarding-news/2017-burton-us-open-snowboarding-championships-return-vail-feb-27-march-4/','https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/history/','https://www.aspentimes.com/sports/from-vermont-to-vail-a-look-back-at-the-36-year-history-of-the-burton-u-s-open-returning-march-5-10/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2018', 'us-open-snowboarding--2018', '36th Burton US Open (2018)', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2018, '2018-03-05', '2018-03-10', 'contest', 'First post-PyeongChang edition. Zoi Sadowski-Synnott and Red Gerard won slopestyle; Maddie Mastro and Scotty James won halfpipe.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Vail Mountain', 'Vail', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://events.burton.com/burton-us-open/event-schedule/','https://www.vailvalleypartnership.com/tag/burton-us-open/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2019', 'us-open-snowboarding--2019', '37th Burton US Open (2019)', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2019, '2019-02-25', '2019-03-02', 'contest', 'Halfpipe and slopestyle for men and women plus a junior jam for riders under 15.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Vail Mountain', 'Vail', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://kingsnowboard.com/blogs/news-1/37th-burton-u-c2-b7s-c2-b7open-vail','https://www.vailvalleypartnership.com/tag/burton-us-open/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2020', 'us-open-snowboarding--2020', '38th Burton US Open (2020)', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2020, '2020-02-24', '2020-02-29', 'contest', 'The last US Open held. Run about four months after Jake Burton Carpenter''s death and dedicated to him. USD 373,000 prize purse. Junior jam halfpipe 2020-02-25; slopestyle finals 2020-02-28; halfpipe finals 2020-02-29.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Golden Peak, Vail Mountain', 'Vail', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.thesebastianvail.com/guide-2020-burton-u-s-open/','https://www.vaildaily.com/news/is-vails-burton-us-open-competition-gone-for-good/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('us-open-snowboarding--2021', 'us-open-snowboarding--2021', '2021 Burton US Open (cancelled)', 'us-open-snowboarding', 2021, '2021-03-01', '2021-03-06', 'contest', 'Scheduled for 2021-03-01 to 2021-03-06 and cancelled. Burton later confirmed the US Open would not be returning to Vail and pointed to the new Burton Mystery Series, intended to be hosted in a different country each time. Vail had invested USD 490,000 in the 2020 event and did not budget for 2022.', 'verified', 'cancelled', 'Cancelled; the event did not return to Vail afterwards.', 'day', 'Vail Mountain', 'Vail', 'USA', NULL, ARRAY['https://www.vaildaily.com/news/is-vails-burton-us-open-competition-gone-for-good/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('us-snowboarding-grand-prix--2021', 'us-snowboarding-grand-prix--2021', '2021 Toyota U.S. Grand Prix, Copper Mountain (halfpipe World Cup)', 'us-snowboarding-grand-prix', 2021, '2021-12-14', NULL, 'contest', 'FIS reported the snowboard halfpipe World Cup at this Toyota U.S. Grand Prix on 14 December 2021. Only the halfpipe date was confirmed; the full run of the Grand Prix week at Copper was not established.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Copper Mountain Resort', 'Copper Mountain, Colorado', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.fis-ski.com/snowboard-park-and-pipe/news/2021-22/toyota-us-grand-prix-halfpipe-world-cup-at-copper-mountain-snowboard']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('usasa-national-championships--1990', 'usasa-national-championships--1990', '1990 USASA National Championships', 'usasa-national-championships', 1990, '1990-02', '1990-02', 'contest', 'Snowboarder/TransWorld 1990s timeline: February 1990 at Snow Valley, California; a severe snowstorm stranded competitors and USASA president Chuck Allen led the rescue. No podium found. City given as Running Springs, California (Snow Valley''s town) - not confirmed in the sources opened. Not to be confused with Snow Valley, Vermont, which hosted the 1983 and 1984 National Snowboarding Championships.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'month', 'Snow Valley', 'Running Springs', 'USA', NULL, ARRAY['https://www.snowboarder.com/news/snowboard-history-timeline-part-31990s']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('usasa-national-championships--2023', 'usasa-national-championships--2023', '2023 USASA National Championships', 'usasa-national-championships', 2023, '2023-03-31', '2023-04-06', 'contest', 'Snowboard championships ran March 31-April 6, 2023; the freeski championships followed April 8-12, 2023. About 1,500 snowboard and freeski competitors attended in total.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Copper Mountain', 'Copper Mountain, Colorado', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','boardercross','giant-slalom','slalom','rail-jam']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.townoffrisco.com/event/copper-mountain-events/usasa-snowboard-national-championships/','https://www.townoffrisco.com/event/copper-mountain-events/usasa-freeski-national-championships/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('usasa-national-championships--2025', 'usasa-national-championships--2025', '2025 USASA National Championships', 'usasa-national-championships', 2025, '2025-03-30', '2025-04-03', 'contest', 'Full championship window March 28-April 9, 2025; snowboard competition March 30-April 3 and freeski April 6-9. Daily formats are confirmed nightly at the Team Captains Meeting.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Copper Mountain', 'Copper Mountain, Colorado', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','boardercross','giant-slalom','slalom','rail-jam']::text[], ARRAY['https://usasa.org/national-championships/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('usasa-national-championships--2026', 'usasa-national-championships--2026', '2026 USASA National Championships', 'usasa-national-championships', 2026, '2026-03-28', '2026-04-02', 'contest', 'Dates from an events listing, not from USASA directly; disciplines for this specific edition not confirmed from the organiser.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Copper Mountain', 'Copper Mountain, Colorado', 'USA', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle','boardercross','giant-slalom','slalom','rail-jam']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.boardriding.com/events/usasa-national-championships-copper-mountain-2026']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('vans-triple-crown-of-snowboarding--2000', 'vans-triple-crown-of-snowboarding--2000', '1999/2000 Vans Triple Crown of Snowboarding', 'vans-triple-crown-of-snowboarding', 2000, '1999-12-03', '2000-02-27', 'contest', 'Three stops: Breckenridge, Colorado 3-5 December 1999 (boardercross, big air with a USD 10,000 winner''s cheque, halfpipe); Mount Seymour, British Columbia 14-16 January 2000 (snowboard cross, halfpipe); Sierra-at-Tahoe, California 25-27 February 2000 (halfpipe). Overall titles to Ross Powers and Ina Poetzl, with a USD 10,000 overall prize.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', NULL, NULL, 'multiple', ARRAY['halfpipe','big-air','boardercross']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.mountainzone.com/snowboarding/2000/vans/index.html','https://www.mountainzone.com/snowboarding/2000/vans/breckenridge/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('waengl-taengl--2012', 'waengl-taengl--2012', '10th Vans Waengl Taengl presented by G-SHOCK', 'waengl-taengl', 2012, '2012-03-17', '2012-03-24', 'contest', 'Tenth-anniversary edition, a week-long ''contest-ival'' billed as the world''s largest snowboard team competition, with team skate, open-air concerts, parties and art installations alongside. Organised by the Aesthetiker.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Mayrhofen', 'Mayrhofen, Zillertal', 'Austria', ARRAY['team','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.vice.com/de/article/waengl-taengl-ueberrollt-mayrhofen/','https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/news/the-asthetikers-announce-a-break-from-the-wangl-tangl-in-2013/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('waengl-taengl--2013', 'waengl-taengl--2013', 'Waengl Taengl 2013 (not held)', 'waengl-taengl', 2013, '2013', NULL, 'contest', 'The crew said they would instead focus on youth development and new event formats.', 'verified', 'cancelled', 'The Aesthetiker announced a break from producing the event in 2013. Club president Steve Gruber: ''we felt we needed time to look at how we could step it up again to guarantee the next edition of the Waengl is kick arse, not an anti-climax.''', 'year', NULL, 'Mayrhofen, Zillertal', 'Austria', NULL, ARRAY['https://www.worldsnowboardfederation.org/news/the-asthetikers-announce-a-break-from-the-wangl-tangl-in-2013/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('westbeach-classic--2000', 'westbeach-classic--2000', '2000 WestBeach Classic', 'series_1774838253156_mep0c', 2000, '2000', NULL, 'contest', 'Final edition. Moved out of the World Ski & Snowboard Festival to the May long weekend. Reported in 2001 by Pique Newsmagazine as the last running.', 'unverified', 'held', NULL, 'year', 'Whistler Blackcomb', 'Whistler', 'Canada', ARRAY['big-air']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.piquenewsmagazine.com/local-sports/westbeach-classic-not-on-2459602']::text[], 'likely'),
  ('westbeach-classic--2001', 'westbeach-classic--2001', '2001 WestBeach Classic', 'series_1774838253156_mep0c', 2001, '2001', NULL, 'contest', 'The Masters Group organised both the WestBeach Classic and the World Snowboarding Championship.', 'verified', 'cancelled', 'Not held. WestBeach Sports redirected its funding to sponsor the World Snowboarding Championship instead; company president Steve Dewar told Pique the brand opportunity was ''too good to pass up''.', 'year', NULL, 'Whistler', 'Canada', NULL, ARRAY['https://www.piquenewsmagazine.com/local-sports/westbeach-classic-not-on-2459602']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('whistler-blackcomb-fis-snowboard-world-cup--2001', 'whistler-blackcomb-fis-snowboard-world-cup--2001', '2001 FIS Snowboard World Cup, Whistler', 'whistler-blackcomb-fis-snowboard-world-cup', 2001, '2001-12-06', '2001-12-11', 'contest', 'Pique Newsmagazine''s 2001 year in sports records snowboard cross, two halfpipes, alpine and big air over these dates, with Guillaume Morisset taking a bronze, Natasza Zurek a silver and Jasey-Jay Anderson a silver in parallel giant slalom. Belongs to the 2001-02 season.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Whistler Blackcomb', 'Whistler', 'Canada', ARRAY['boardercross','halfpipe','parallel-giant-slalom','big-air']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.piquenewsmagazine.com/local-sports/whistler-the-year-in-sports-2461092']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('winsport-calgary-world-cup--2019', 'winsport-calgary-world-cup--2019', '2019 Halfpipe Rodeo FIS Ski & Snowboard World Cup', 'winsport-calgary-world-cup', 2019, '2019-02-13', '2019-02-16', 'contest', 'Announced by Canada Snowboard in November 2018 and listed on its 2018-19 domestic calendar.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Canada Olympic Park', 'Calgary', 'Canada', ARRAY['halfpipe']::text[], ARRAY['https://www.canadasnowboard.ca/en/news/?id=1256','https://www.canadasnowboard.ca/en/news/?id=1259']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('winsport-calgary-world-cup--2020', 'winsport-calgary-world-cup--2020', '2020 FIS Freestyle Ski and Snowboard World Cups, Calgary', 'winsport-calgary-world-cup', 2020, '2020-02-12', '2020-02-16', 'contest', 'Part of a season in which Canada hosted a World Cup in every snowboard discipline.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Canada Olympic Park', 'Calgary', 'Canada', ARRAY['halfpipe','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://olympic.ca/2019/10/24/winter-competitions-coming-to-canada-in-2019-20/']::text[], 'verified'),
  ('winter-dew-tour--2008', 'winter-dew-tour--2008', '2008-09 Winter Dew Tour, Stop 1: Breckenridge', 'winter-dew-tour', 2008, '2008-12-18', '2008-12-21', 'contest', 'Opening stop of the inaugural Winter Dew Tour. Men''s and women''s snowboard and freeski slopestyle and superpipe; $1.5 million purse across the three stops; Dew Cup awarded to season champions. Belongs to the 2008-09 season.', 'verified', 'held', NULL, 'day', 'Breckenridge Ski Resort', 'Breckenridge, Colorado', 'USA', ARRAY['superpipe','slopestyle']::text[], ARRAY['https://news.vailresorts.com/2008-11-21-WINTER-DEW-TOUR-TO-VISIT-BRECKENRIDGE-RESORT,-DEC-18-21','https://www.saminfo.com/news/sam-headline-news/5336-976-breck-mount-snow-northstar-highlight-dew-tour']::text[], 'verified'),
